You have optic neuritis. This is inflammation of the optic nerve, which is the nerve that carries visual information from the eye to the brain.\
\
When the optic nerve becomes inflamed, vision can become blurred or dim, and colors may appear less vivid. Many people also notice discomfort or pain around the eye, especially when moving the eye.\
\
Optic neuritis often develops suddenly over hours or days. In some cases it occurs on its own, but it can also be associated with conditions that affect the immune system, including multiple sclerosis. Because of this possible association, further medical evaluation is usually recommended.\
\
